class:: PitchStability
summary:: Confidence-weighted pitch spread over a time window
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Pitch
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/Pitch2, Classes/FundamentalCandidates, Classes/PitchDeviation, Classes/Vibrato2

description::
An original statistical descriptor of a supplied pitch trajectory. Frequency is converted to cents relative to 440 Hz; confidence-weighted first and second moments define population variance over the rolling window. Initial estimates use observations collected so far. Unvoiced observations have zero weight; a currently unvoiced input outputs zeros. Vibrato and glissando both increase spread, so this is pitch stability rather than a vibrato classifier. The method is a direct application of weighted variance and contains no borrowed DSP implementation.

Vanilla link::Classes/Lag:: smooths a trajectory. PitchStability measures its spread without modifying the trajectory.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: freq
Supplied control-rate pitch in Hz. Zero or a nonfinite value is excluded.

argument:: confidence
Weight from 0 through 1 for each supplied observation.

argument:: windowTime
Literal rolling window in seconds, 0.05 through 5. Storage is capped at 16384 control samples.

returns::
An Array: stability = exp(-deviationCents / 50), weighted population standard deviation in cents.

examples::
PitchStability computes rolling weighted variance in cents over an observation window, returning an exponential stability metric ($1.0$ for rock-solid pitch, approaching $0.0$ during vibrato, trills, and glissandi). In this example, it gates a lush stereo tape delay: fast melodic transitions stay dry and focused, while long held notes bloom out into warm delay repeats. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: tracks the real-time stability metric.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("melody.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic melody fallback
            Saw.ar(Select.kr(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(0, 5), [220, 261.63, 293.66, 329.63, 392, 440])) * 0.2
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var pitch = PitchMPM.kr(source, 80, 1200, 2048, 0.25);
        var stability = PitchStability.kr(pitch[0], pitch[1], 0.25);
        var isStable = stability[0].lag(0.04);

        // Delay send gated by pitch stability
        var delaySend = source * isStable;
        var delay = CombC.ar(delaySend, 0.5, [0.25, 0.33], 1.8) * 0.35;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + delay;

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, stability[0]) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Pitch Stability", ~miraBus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
